{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the judge shall cause him to fall.</b> This teaches that they do not flog him neither standing nor sitting, but bent over (Makkot 22)." "<b>Before him, according to his wickedness.</b> And behind him twice that — from here they said: they flog him two-thirds from behind him and a third from before him (Sifrei; Makkot 22)." "<b>By number.</b> And it is not pointed בַּמִּסְפָּר — this teaches that it is attached, to say בְּמִסְפַּר אַרְבָּעִים — not forty full ones, but a count that gathers and completes to forty, and they are forty less one (there)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:18.262740657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}